#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166530 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166933 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca890a8e-9ddd-51f7-9784-c9c1f020adef" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Laplace Transform to a System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/id #uuid "008364d3-24bd-58e2-a8ab-f0d4d881e918" :question/math-academy-id "e-21575" :question/problem "![](images/81/8161123eafa5ed80dc37b8e017c5598fcacaf241a84a09ca27f73d204d7b0e74.png)\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, find the system of equations." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{2{x}_{1}(t)+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-3} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{-3{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=2L{{x}_{1}(t)}+5L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)}-3L{1} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=-3L{{x}_{1}(t)}+4L{{x}_{2}(t)}+2L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the results\n\n$$\n\\mathcal L\\{1\\} = \\dfrac{1}{s}, \\quad\n\\mathcal L\\{\\cos(2t)\\} = \\dfrac{s}{s^2+4}, \\quad\n\\mathcal L\\{\\sin(2t)\\} = \\dfrac{2}{s^2+4},\n$$\n\nwe can write our system as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1=2{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{5s}{{s}^{2}+4}-\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+2=-3{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t),$ respectively."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166531 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166934 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b22e449-2966-59cf-b012-3f5721b4bc98" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Laplace Transformed Initial Value Problem"}] :question/id #uuid "230e2550-b584-53fd-9da4-4128584124dc" :question/math-academy-id "e-21576" :question/problem "![](images/ce/ce973be1a5a98fa04fad06c1ca5ee19c7f1b0cfd421d0cd449c7cb52138bf9bd.png)\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $\\mathcal{L}$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$  find the solution of the new system." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{-{x}_{1}(t)+4} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{2{x}_{1}(t)-3{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=-L{{x}_{1}(t)}+4L{1} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=2L{{x}_{1}(t)}-3L{{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1=-{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-0=2{X}_{1}(s)-3{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\},$ and we have used the fact that $\\mathcal L\\{1\\} = \\dfrac1s.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for $X_1(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1 & =-{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ (s+1){X}_{1}(s) & =1+\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ (s+1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{s+4}{s} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{s+4}{s(s+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for $X_2(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s) & =2{X}_{1}(s)-3{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s+3){X}_{2}(s) & =2{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ (s+3){X}_{2}(s) & =2(\\frac{s+4}{s(s+1)}) \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2(s+4)}{s(s+1)(s+3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\nX_1(s) = \\dfrac{s+4}{s(s+1)} ,\\qquad \nX_2(s) = \\dfrac{2(s+4)}{s(s+1)(s+3)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166532 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166935 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff314a2-9059-5a37-8c2c-2b7a2fe6dcd9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"}] :question/id #uuid "748ef205-542b-5763-9cdd-00dc9ff1d181" :question/math-academy-id "e-21577" :question/problem "![](images/a6/a699a4e262534557453aaa9e44d1b273dd4489190e50cec8f9ef9e0da91e7d29.png)\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\nX_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\} = -\\dfrac{1}{s+2} + \\dfrac{2}{s-1} - \\dfrac{2}{s}, \\qquad\nX_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\} = \\dfrac{1}{s+2} + \\dfrac{3}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem." :question/worked-solution "To find $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to $X_1(s)$ and $X_2(s){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{-\\frac{1}{s+2}+\\frac{2}{s-1}-\\frac{2}{s}} \\\\  & =-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}}+2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}}-2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2\\cdot t}+2{e}^{1\\cdot t}-2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2{e}^{t}-{e}^{-2t}-2 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}+\\frac{3}{s}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}}+3\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={e}^{-2\\cdot t}+3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={e}^{-2t}+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{t}-{e}^{-2t}-2 \\\\ {e}^{-2t}+3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305119 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166934 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b22e449-2966-59cf-b012-3f5721b4bc98" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Laplace Transformed Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f80fb1b-d38e-5a24-8d23-a1d10021010e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-{s}^{2}+s+10}{s(s+1)(s-4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303251}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f80fb1b-d38e-5a24-8d23-a1d10021010e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-{s}^{2}+s+10}{s(s+1)(s-4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303251} :answer-field/id #uuid "8acdc256-05ee-570c-8605-17d181b69a3c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304448}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "53d3abf7-a9e9-5b69-8cf5-e63a711cb51d" :question/math-academy-id "q-332784" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+5 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{s+5}{s(s+1)},\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{-{x}_{1}(t)+5} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{2{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=-L{{x}_{1}(t)}+5L{1} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=2L{{x}_{1}(t)}+4L{{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1=-{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{5}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+1=2{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)},$ and we have used the fact that $L{1}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1 & =-{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{5}{s} \\\\ (s+1){X}_{1}(s) & =1+\\frac{5}{s} \\\\ (s+1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{s+5}{s} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{s+5}{s(s+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)+1 & =2{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =2{X}_{1}(s)-1 \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =2(\\frac{s+5}{s(s+1)})-1 \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2(s+5)-s(s+1)}{s(s+1)} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-{s}^{2}+s+10}{s(s+1)} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-{s}^{2}+s+10}{s(s+1)(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system  in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{s+5}{s(s+1)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{-{s}^{2}+s+10}{s(s+1)(s-4)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305121 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166933 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca890a8e-9ddd-51f7-9784-c9c1f020adef" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Laplace Transform to a System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "045d4f87-c09d-56c8-bf90-3aae549a88a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{6}{{s}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302483} {:answer/id #uuid "1d75587e-be36-5b40-a1fe-0f3749cf3694" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{6}{{s}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302647} {:answer/id #uuid "42c0834c-6f4f-5076-bd1c-e26df24308cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{3}{{s}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302877} {:answer/id #uuid "8643a835-a8b1-56d3-9f3c-b3643d0944dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{4}{{s}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303292}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "045d4f87-c09d-56c8-bf90-3aae549a88a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{6}{{s}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302483} :answer-field/id #uuid "0624d020-8bd2-53ed-8ffd-4738bf877016" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304079} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6319f140-0878-5d34-b5c4-fed8a78f1e40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s{X}_{1}(s)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303058} {:answer/id #uuid "d9d05387-d444-5c10-b95a-a77f34e5fb53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{X}_{1}(s)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303811} {:answer/id #uuid "db946fa8-a5bf-50ac-9337-1f49fe56e5c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s{X}_{1}(s)+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303824} {:answer/id #uuid "dd517d0b-8e21-54c1-9f20-8f3f2a9627d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{X}_{1}(s)+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6319f140-0878-5d34-b5c4-fed8a78f1e40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s{X}_{1}(s)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303058} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d0f55e6-615e-5589-8583-791c7c78ee7a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304245} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "372171ce-5c21-5fb2-964a-57cb6d756845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302799} {:answer/id #uuid "64e25b69-fb0b-58c9-bb85-f7c4c1c1964b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303070} {:answer/id #uuid "82ac8fa2-cadc-50d8-82da-d554595934c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303272} {:answer/id #uuid "c4007cf6-f03a-5099-aa50-99917a6d166f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82ac8fa2-cadc-50d8-82da-d554595934c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303272} :answer-field/id #uuid "571b82f8-3f2d-5456-bb83-188a9b88182f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304314}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "158ccd60-79bd-5986-bdf7-58471b693523" :question/math-academy-id "q-332796" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+3{t}^{2}+1 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)-2,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, we get the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{{field-1}}={{field-2}}+\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+1=-{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)-{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{{x}_{1}(t)+3{t}^{2}+1} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{-{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)-2}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}+3L{{t}^{2}}+L{1} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=-L{{x}_{1}(t)}+4L{{x}_{2}(t)}-2L{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the results\n\n$$\nL{1}=\\frac{1}{s},\\,L{{t}^{2}}=\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}},\n$$\n\n we can write our system as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1={X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{6}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+1=-{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)-\\frac{2}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167233 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166935 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff314a2-9059-5a37-8c2c-2b7a2fe6dcd9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "d27e42ca-cf51-537c-93bc-c24a5d179100" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164464} {:answer-field/id #uuid "6a0fa9d7-a6e9-5102-9558-03b18008e8b7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164465}] :question/id #uuid "63d4e608-bf55-5ffd-acb6-0fb6294a7841" :question/math-academy-id "q-333131" :question/problem "${x_{1}^{′}(t) = x_{1}(t) + 4x_{2}(t) + 9; x_{2}^{′}(t) = 3x_{2}(t) + 6,x(0) = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution\n$X_{1}(s) = L{x_{1}(t)} = \\frac{1}{s - 1} + \\frac{2}{s - 3} - \\frac{1}{s}, X_{2}(s) = L{x_{2}(t)} = \\frac{1}{s - 3} - \\frac{2}{s}$.\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t) =$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308392 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166935 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff314a2-9059-5a37-8c2c-2b7a2fe6dcd9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74c732f2-4f86-504b-8cdd-aa1fa2e5c7f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{t}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306262}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74c732f2-4f86-504b-8cdd-aa1fa2e5c7f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{t}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306262} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d7b7b8a-07e2-5e92-88b6-369bfe5faec3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307916} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14a9d938-5d30-5c6c-b0a5-7c4e863e76a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{t}-1+2{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14a9d938-5d30-5c6c-b0a5-7c4e863e76a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{t}-1+2{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305329} :answer-field/id #uuid "faba9d5a-e4bb-5a2a-b64b-592a4e00c589" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308320}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0f0cc0f3-9d0f-5e89-ae11-bc48a4d849b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-333137" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+9{x}_{2}(t)-20 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{2}(t)-2,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{2}{s+2}+\\frac{3}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s-1}+\\frac{2}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{s+2}+\\frac{3}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & =2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}}+3\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & =2{e}^{-2\\cdot t}+3{e}^{1\\cdot t}-1 \\\\  & =3{e}^{t}-1+2{e}^{-2t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}+\\frac{2}{s}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}}+2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={e}^{1\\cdot t}+2 \\\\  & ={e}^{t}+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{t}-1+2{e}^{-2t} \\\\ {e}^{t}+2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
